1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,520
-Do you even realize you’ve been  acting super weird?

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:03,240
-How?

3
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:04,680
-Ouch!

4
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,280
-Coach Kong told me you’re dropping out.

5
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:09,520
-What are you doing?

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,400
-You should be glad

7
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,720
-you won’t have to see me anymore.

8
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:15,680
-If I told you the truth,

9
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:17,400
-would you change your mind?

10
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:26,120
When you said you love me,

11
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,720
what kind of love was it?

12
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:57,360
What do you feel about me?

13
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:08,120
I...

14
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:08,920
(Sun!)

15
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:15,280
Yes, Pa?

16
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:17,800
I just came to tell you

17
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:20,360
that the toilet on the second floor is clogged.

18
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,840
Use the one downstairs instead.

19
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:25,920
Yes, Pa.

20
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:30,560
What about us?

21
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:31,520
Shhh!

22
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:34,680
This is not the time.

23
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:36,040
You wanna die?

24
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:37,640
Go, leave.

25
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:38,800
Uh, Sun!

26
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:39,800
Yes, Pa?

27
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,240
Don’t stay up late.

28
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:46,800
Yes, Pa.

29
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,040
I’m going to sleep now.

30
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:50,680
Yeah.

31
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,480
(Will you play doubles with me?)

32
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:10,400
SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT OF CULTURAL PROMOTION,
MINISTRY OF CULTURE

33
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:26,480
So, about you dropping out…

34
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,800
I’m not dropping out anymore.

35
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,240
And also...

36
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:46,520
I’d like to play doubles with Bay again.

37
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,320
What about you, Bay?

38
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,040
Me, too.

39
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:56,640
This is what I’m talking about!

40
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:58,720
Now…

41
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,720
I hope you two can sync up soon.

42
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:02,440
Yes, sir.

43
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,720
Of course.

44
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:10,840
You’re late.

45
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:13,240
Sorry.

46
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:17,160
Just a bun and a box of shumai.

47
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,600
Is this worth the delivery fees?

48
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,320
Well, this is all I wanna eat.

49
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:22,760
Why are you complaining?

50
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:23,680
You didn’t have to deliver it yourself.

51
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:24,800
Just pay.

52
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:27,880
Hurry.

53
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,640
Hey, about the other day at the hospital…

54
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:33,440
What you asked me…

55
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:33,960
Mmm.

56
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,680
The principal had Bay and Sun

57
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,080
compete in PREM’S GAME.

58
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:41,160
Like…together.

59
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:42,240
Doubles?

60
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,000
Uh-huh.

61
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:46,320
And…they both agreed.

62
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:50,920
That’s good.

63
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:51,840
Uh-huh.

64
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:54,120
But...

65
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,680
I think we should…

66
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,680
help each other...

67
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,160
keep this from you dad.

68
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,120
I can understand that.

69
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:07,000
If the parents find out about this,

70
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,280
the boys will feel pressured again.

71
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:11,000
But they have to practice together, right?

72
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,440
How could we keep this a secret?

73
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,920
The principal gave us a budget

74
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,560
for the kids to go practice out of town.

75
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,120
Are you...

76
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,400
interested in...

77
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:23,880
coming along to help me babysit?

78
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,400
Babysit?

79
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:25,920
Well…

80
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,080
these kids aren’t easy to handle.

81
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,400
If I had someone to help me,

82
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,400
that’d be great.

83
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:33,560
To take care of you?

84
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,480
Yes, to take care of me…

85
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:35,560
No, I mean the kids!

86
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:38,840
Will you come?

87
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:42,040
Please?

88
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,400
If I have to go alone,

89
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:45,880
it’ll be so hard for me.

90
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:47,440
Aren’t you worried about me?

91
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:50,360
Fine, I’ll go.

92
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,000
Yes!

93
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:56,160
This way Bay will have an excuse

94
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,120
to go out of town.

95
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,040
Great.

96
00:06:58,600 --> 00:06:59,560
Thank you so much.

97
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:02,840
I’ll send you the details via LINE.

98
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,280
You still use the same account, right?

99
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:07,320
Mmm.

100
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:08,640
Text me.

101
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:10,160
I’ll go then.

102
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,200
See you.

103
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:12,800
Drive safely.

104
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:19,880
And check your LINE.

105
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:53,120
Hey!

106
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:53,880
Hey.

107
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,960
What are you doing?!

108
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,240
You’re early today.

109
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:13,720
What’s the matter with you?

110
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:15,160
Are you sick?

111
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,240
No.

112
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,800
He’s been sitting like this for 15 minutes.

113
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:20,640
Eh?

114
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:22,720
If you’re not sick, get up and go warm up.

115
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:23,800
Go.

116
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,960
Get up now.

117
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:29,840
Go on.

118
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:33,560
-Hey!
-Hey!

119
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,680
Are you okay?

120
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:35,560
Sun?

121
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,160
What’s wrong with you?

122
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,680
If someone confessed they liked you,

123
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,520
what would you do?

124
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,040
Who confessed?

125
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:56,520
I barely see you talk to anyone.

126
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,800
Hmm.

127
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,320
If I liked them,

128
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,280
I’d say ‘yes’, if not I’d just say ‘no’.

129
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:04,480
Yeah, right.

130
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:08,040
What if you don’t know if you like them or not?

131
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:09,520
Just say ‘no’ then!

132
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:11,280
Because if you liked them,
you would know.

133
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:12,760
Hey, are you crazy?!

134
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,360
How could I just say ‘no’?

135
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,720
It’s like I’m missing out on an opportunity,
right?

136
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,640
If you’re not feeling it,

137
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:17,720
that means you don’t like them.

138
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,160
Period.

139
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:23,600
What if you think you do,

140
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:28,160
but the voice in your head says

141
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,160
“This is not possible.”?

142
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,600
I can’t decide for you.

143
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,920
If you choose to date them and it works out,

144
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,200
I’m happy for you.

145
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:41,360
But if you know from the jump
that it’s not possible,

146
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,680
it’ll be better if you don’t start it at all.

147
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,080
Holy cow!

148
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:50,600
This kind of thing takes time.

149
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,400
You have to really get to know each other

150
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:53,840
before you decide

151
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,040
if they’re right for you.

152
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:57,680
You think so, Zippo?!

153
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,080
I know so, brother.

154
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,400
Just let them in.

155
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,520
If you like them,

156
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,320
everything will become possible.

157
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:04,080
Really?

158
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,080
-Really.
-But...

159
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,120
What if I realize later that I don’t like them?

160
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,040
Then just call it quits.

161
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:08,720
Period.

162
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:11,560
I’m not asking you for advice anymore, Keaw.

163
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:13,240
From now on

164
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,040
I will only talk to my boy Zippo.

165
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,320
Best bro forever!

166
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,960
Best bro forever!

167
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:19,160
Hey!

168
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:22,120
If you already had the answer,

169
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,280
why would you even ask me?

170
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:23,920
I didn’t have the answer.

171
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,000
You did.

172
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:25,520
I didn’t.

173
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:25,760
Did!

174
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:26,200
Didn’t!

175
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:26,520
Did!

176
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:26,960
Didn’t!

177
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:27,200
Did!

178
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:27,760
Didn’t!

179
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:28,400
-Please, the audacity!
-I didn’t!

180
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,440
-Enough!
-I didn’t.

181
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,520
Just go practice!

182
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:31,560
Go!

183
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:34,680
I didn’t.

184
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,320
I said go practice!

185
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:37,320
-Best bro.
-Keaw!

186
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:38,120
I can’t with him!

187
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:38,840
-Keaw!
-I can’t with him!

188
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:43,720
Hey, Bay.

189
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:46,600
Why didn’t you come to practice today?

190
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,640
I had to help Petong with his portfolio.

191
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:49,760
Right.

192
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:52,320
Are you two gonna compete again

193
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,360
over how to get home?

194
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,560
I see.

195
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:26,840
Don’t even say a thing.

196
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:27,880
Nah…

197
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:29,640
I see.

198
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:31,640
Oh…

199
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:34,240
I have to go meet Minami’s brother today.

200
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,480
We wanted to talk it out.

201
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:36,840
I’ll see you later.

202
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:37,280
Yeah.

203
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:38,760
You go.

204
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,040
You two get home safe.

205
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:41,000
Yeah, yeah. We can go home by ourselves.

206
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,160
-Get it, bro, get it!
-Just go.

207
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:42,960
Yeah, go.

208
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:43,440
You can do it.

209
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:43,720
Yeah.

210
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:44,480
-I’ll go, bye.
-See you.

211
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:51,080
Since there’s no winner today,

212
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,480
wanna go home together?

213
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:01,400
Come on.

214
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:48,600
Is this yours, Sun?

215
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:51,320
Yes, Pa.

216
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:54,520
It’s for me.

217
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:55,960
Oh, you…

218
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:58,080
Are you sure you don’t want me
to drive you?

219
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:00,080
It’s okay, Pa.

220
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,240
I called a ride.

221
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:05,760
Before you do anything dangerous,
think about your Pa.

222
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,120
Why would you say that, Pa?

223
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:13,080
Well…

224
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,320
I’ve seen on the news

225
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:19,000
that some kids who went to the beach
died from drowning.

226
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:23,600
Think about me before you decide
to go into deep water.

227
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:24,920
Okay, Pa.

228
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:26,400
Don’t worry.

229
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:29,080
I’ll only go knee-deep into the water.

230
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:30,400
Good.

231
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,200
Goodbye, Pa.

232
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,440
Chun!

233
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:44,000
Your feng shui mirror is reflecting
toward my restaurant.

234
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:46,440
Do you want to blind my customers?

235
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:47,200
Remove it!

236
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:51,920
They said this mirror helps reflect evil energy.

237
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:53,280
Apparently, it’s working.

238
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,400
It’s really working.

239
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:55,600
Hey, you bastard.

240
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,280
-Hey!
-What?

241
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,880
You’re causing trouble for other people.

242
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,840
You should have some common sense, Chun.

243
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,120
So? So what?!

244
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,040
If you have a problem, just move away!

245
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:05,160
You asshole.

246
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:08,320
That way people won’t have to hear you

247
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:11,280
yelling or bragging about your son,

248
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,600
or whatever nonsense you do.

249
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:16,480
Oh, so you’re jealous?

250
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,000
To see that my sons are successful.

251
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:22,240
Unlike yours, who got removed from
the tennis tryout.

252
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:22,560
Hey…

253
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:24,800
Don’t talk about my son!

254
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:25,600
And what, huh?

255
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:27,080
You want it? I warned you!

256
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,000
Pa, that’s enough.

257
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,000
Come on then.

258
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:29,840
Come on!

259
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,840
I’m waiting.

260
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,280
You’re lucky my son’s holding me back.

261
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,240
For my son’s sake…

262
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,080
That’s enough, Pa.

263
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,440
You’re so hotheaded, huh?

264
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:36,440
You are hotheaded!

265
00:14:56,920 --> 00:14:57,320
Don’t…

266
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,880
Don’t you come one step closer.

267
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,240
Oh, come on. Come to me, Chun.

268
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,520
I’m already here.

269
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:04,800
Bring it on.

270
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:08,920
CHARTERED BUS

271
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,120
Good morning.

272
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:15,600
Good morning, teacher.

273
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:16,520
“Good morning, teacher”?

274
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,120
Get to your seat.

275
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:20,200
I can’t with you guys.

276
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,400
Where are you gonna sit?

277
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,320
Morning, Coach.

278
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:25,360
Morning.

279
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:28,480
Hey.

280
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:29,640
You’re coming, too?

281
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,680
I asked Boat to help me look after
you guys.

282
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,120
You kids are so chaotic

283
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:36,280
I can’t watch you all by myself.

284
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:38,720
Go find your seat.

285
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:50,720
Good morning.

286
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:51,520
Good morning, Coach.

287
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,280
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

288
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,280
Go get a seat.

289
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:56,000
Good morning, guys.

290
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,280
Is this all?

291
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:00,400
What’s up, Sun?

292
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:02,000
-Hi.
-We’re missing one person.

293
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:02,640
Petong.

294
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:06,200
I’m here.

295
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,360
-Hello.
-Good morning, Coach.

296
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:07,800
Good morning.

297
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:08,920
-Sit down.
-Morning, guys.

298
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:10,240
Scoot over.

299
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:11,960
Hey.

300
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:13,840
What are you doing here?

301
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:15,000
I have no idea.

302
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,840
Since everyone’s going,
I wanted to go, too.

303
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,200
Let’s go!

304
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:21,000
Start rolling.

305
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:21,680
Door closing.

306
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:53,120
I got the keycards.

307
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,480
Where are Ally and Keaw?

308
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,200
Having a photoshoot.

309
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:55,760
Photoshoot?

310
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:58,280
I’ll get the memory full already.

311
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,760
I got your keycards, Ally and Keaw.

312
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:01,320
Let’s go.

313
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:03,000
They’re not playing.

314
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:04,720
Here’s your keycard.

315
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:05,280
You two stay together.

316
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:06,080
Okay.

317
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:09,120
You stay with Coach Kong then.

318
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:12,200
Old men stick together, right?

319
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,080
Your dad is old!

320
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:15,120
Hey, wait, wait, wait.

321
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:17,360
We share the same dad.

322
00:17:19,120 --> 00:17:20,800
Don’t you remember?

323
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:21,840
He’s the only old one.

324
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:22,680
I’m not old yet.

325
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:23,840
You’re old, too.

326
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:25,840
Just kidding, Coach.

327
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:27,120
Then I’ll stay with…

328
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:28,040
I’m staying with Zippo.

329
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:29,920
Is that so?

330
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:31,640
Your keycard.

331
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:33,240
Thank you, Coach.

332
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:36,280
So Bay, you…

333
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:37,640
stay with Petong, okay?

334
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:39,800
Your keycard.

335
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:43,960
Now, everyone go unpack.

336
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:45,120
See you in half an hour.

337
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:46,480
Better start practicing soon

338
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,640
since we don’t have much time today.

339
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:48,280
Yes, Coach.

340
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:49,520
If you’re late, we won’t have time
to play in the water.

341
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:50,800
Okay, coming.

342
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:00,360
It’s good you’re staying with me.

343
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:01,720
It’s gonna be a long night.

344
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:02,280
Let’s go.

345
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:10,800
Now, kids,

346
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:11,560
you’re ready?

347
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:12,960
Yes!

348
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,040
Good.

349
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:15,520
Zippo!

350
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:16,680
Yes?

351
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,320
Aren’t you joining PREM’S GAME?

352
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:18,880
What?

353
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,200
I’m competing, too?

354
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:23,760
Haven’t I told you

355
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:27,720
I wanted you to take Sun’s place
in PREM’S GAME?

356
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:30,920
Uhh, you haven’t.

357
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:34,360
Well…

358
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:35,600
Congratulations!

359
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:38,680
Zippo will play singles in PREM’S GAME!

360
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:40,360
Yes!

361
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,160
I get to compete, too, Ally.

362
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,160
Sun. Keaw.

363
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:44,720
Go, get ready.

364
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:45,320
Go.

365
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:54,840
Good.

366
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:57,080
Go lower.

367
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:58,320
Please move.

368
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:00,360
What is this, sir?

369
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,840
Yes, nice. Good job.

370
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:03,640
Well done.

371
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:10,680
Focus!

372
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:22,040
Ally.

373
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:23,160
Hmm?

374
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,200
Do you think they are…

375
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:28,240
Oh, I clocked it.

376
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:06,280
What’s up with you two today?

377
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:08,480
You’re not in sync at all.

378
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:14,640
It’s nothing, Coach.

379
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,800
I just have a lot on my mind.

380
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:33,160
Sun.

381
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:35,920
What you said the other day…

382
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:38,400
It was about Bay, right?

383
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:38,960
Hey.

384
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:41,200
You can tell?

385
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:43,240
Even I can tell.

386
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:45,920
Why don’t you just talk it out?

387
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:52,000
Didn’t you say it yourself?

388
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:55,080
If you don’t think it’s possible,

389
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:57,800
why bother starting it?

390
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:58,320
Hey.

391
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,520
You’re playing together but you’re not talking?

392
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:03,000
We only talk about the game.

393
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:05,760
I can be professional.

394
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:22,200
If you really care about him,

395
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,000
you should talk to him.

396
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:26,040
How can I?

397
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,080
Boat is on this trip, too.

398
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:32,360
What would I do if he told his dad?

399
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,280
Just find the right moment.

400
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,440
They’re not together all the time.

401
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:37,480
Just try.

402
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,240
Have the talk.

403
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,120
Don’t you look so proud?

404
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,680
They’re my trainees.

405
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:32,280
How do you feel about playing tennis
with Sun again?

406
00:22:38,120 --> 00:22:43,760
Actually, it was great when we
were practicing at first.

407
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:51,160
But I guess I’m the one who messed it up.

408
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:56,960
What did you do?

409
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,200
I might have crossed the line.

410
00:23:04,760 --> 00:23:06,160
I deserve to be hated.

411
00:23:24,120 --> 00:23:24,760
Can we talk?

412
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:30,120
Then talk.

413
00:23:33,640 --> 00:23:34,320
What’s up with you?

414
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:36,400
Why are you here alone?

415
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:39,040
What’s going on with you?

416
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:41,400
You’ve been avoiding me all day.

417
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:44,040
Well, I don’t know how to act.

418
00:23:45,600 --> 00:23:47,080
I don’t even know how I feel.

419
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,680
All I know is I’m not mad at you.

420
00:23:56,240 --> 00:24:00,600
I’m so glad I get to play with you again.

421
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:04,640
You’re glad?

422
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:07,720
Then why are you acting like this?

423
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:12,640
Because Boat is here, too.

424
00:24:13,280 --> 00:24:14,520
What if he tells your dad?

425
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,480
Boat knows I like you.

426
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:22,600
And he’s fine with that?

427
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:24,080
He is.

428
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:27,680
And even if he weren’t,

429
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:30,080
I wouldn’t care.

430
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:38,000
It’s that easy for you, huh?

431
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:42,640
It’s not easy.

432
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:45,200
But when I like someone,

433
00:24:46,280 --> 00:24:47,720
I’m willing to give it my all.

434
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:56,040
But do you really think this is possible?

435
00:25:02,040 --> 00:25:03,000
Do you like me, Sun?

436
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:07,760
If you like me too,

437
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:10,920
I’m willing to get through any obstacle.

438
00:25:14,400 --> 00:25:15,000
I don’t know.

439
00:25:20,640 --> 00:25:21,640
I’m still not sure.

440
00:25:25,480 --> 00:25:26,520
It feels great…

441
00:25:28,680 --> 00:25:29,680
knowing that you like me.

442
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:35,760
But does this mean I like you too?

443
00:25:38,160 --> 00:25:39,120
I’m still not sure.

444
00:25:41,200 --> 00:25:41,840
Then…

445
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,400
will you let me try to win you over

446
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:48,520
until you’re sure about your feelings?

447
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:52,840
♪ Ever since that day ♪

448
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:57,080
♪ When you and I happened to meet ♪

449
00:25:57,080 --> 00:25:59,520
♪ It’s like a dream ♪

450
00:25:59,520 --> 00:26:00,920
♪ ’Cause you’re the one ♪

451
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:04,840
♪ Who came along and made my heart skip a beat ♪

452
00:26:04,840 --> 00:26:10,160
♪ It feels like I’ve finally found love ♪

453
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:10,880
You can try.

454
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:15,600
There!

455
00:26:16,640 --> 00:26:17,200
You said it!

456
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:18,360
You’ll let me?!

457
00:26:18,600 --> 00:26:19,200
Quiet. People will…

458
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:20,880
-Woohoo!!
-They will hear you.

459
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:21,960
I’m allowed to make a move on you!

460
00:26:21,960 --> 00:26:22,680
Bay!

461
00:26:22,680 --> 00:26:23,320
Woohoo!

462
00:26:23,440 --> 00:26:24,320
I’ll make a move on you every second.

463
00:26:24,320 --> 00:26:25,120
Keep it down.

464
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:25,800
Woohoo!

465
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:26,040
Bay!

466
00:26:26,040 --> 00:26:27,080
People are staring.

467
00:26:27,080 --> 00:26:28,200
-Be quiet!
-Sun!

468
00:26:28,280 --> 00:26:30,240
I’ll keep trying until I can make you
my boyfriend.

469
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:31,160
-You hear that?!
-Damn it.

470
00:26:31,160 --> 00:26:32,760
-They’re all looking at us.
-Sun!

471
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:33,720
Woohoo!

472
00:26:33,720 --> 00:26:34,720
Keep it down!

473
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:37,440
I’ll keep trying every second.

474
00:26:37,440 --> 00:26:38,560
Bay, keep it down!

475
00:26:38,720 --> 00:26:39,320
Hey.

476
00:26:47,600 --> 00:26:49,240
Morning, my tofu.

477
00:27:12,320 --> 00:27:13,720
These remind me of back then.

478
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:17,240
Do you still remember

479
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:19,160
when we were young,

480
00:27:19,560 --> 00:27:21,160
I beat you in running every time.

481
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:22,880
It was just a warm-up run.

482
00:27:23,520 --> 00:27:25,240
Who takes it as a competition?

483
00:27:25,600 --> 00:27:26,520
A loss is a loss.

484
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:27,880
I’ll beat you today then.

485
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:28,960
Well, you can try.

486
00:27:30,080 --> 00:27:31,280
Hey! Wait up!

487
00:27:31,280 --> 00:27:32,720
Hey! Wait!

488
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:34,320
Hey! Sun!

489
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:44,200
-Oops.
-Hey.

490
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:48,160
Hey! Hold on.

491
00:27:48,600 --> 00:27:49,160
What?

492
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:53,680
You haven’t been working out at all,
have you?

493
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:56,640
I only need these for sculpting.

494
00:28:00,080 --> 00:28:01,360
You go on.

495
00:28:02,080 --> 00:28:03,160
I’ll wait here.

496
00:28:03,720 --> 00:28:04,680
Just come get me later.

497
00:28:05,200 --> 00:28:06,120
No way.

498
00:28:07,720 --> 00:28:08,160
Come on.

499
00:28:10,320 --> 00:28:11,720
I’m too tired.

500
00:28:13,680 --> 00:28:15,080
I’m too tired.

501
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:25,680
Hey!

502
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:26,640
Come on.

503
00:28:27,680 --> 00:28:28,720
Let’s keep running.

504
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:31,360
Okay, keep running.

505
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:32,840
Come on.

506
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:41,720
Take this!

507
00:28:41,880 --> 00:28:42,080
Here.

508
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:46,280
There.

509
00:28:47,360 --> 00:28:48,760
Here we go.

510
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:50,440
It’s happening.

511
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:53,520
I’ll keep my fingers crossed for
this year’s PREM’S GAME.

512
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:55,200
Aren’t you keeping your fingers crossed
for the singles as well?

513
00:28:57,160 --> 00:28:57,840
I am.

514
00:28:58,400 --> 00:28:59,600
But for a different reason.

515
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:00,000
Oh.

516
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:00,880
different reason.

517
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:08,360
Don’t hold back.

518
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:11,520
I’m here to support you.

519
00:29:39,120 --> 00:29:40,040
Your shoelaces.

520
00:29:44,280 --> 00:29:45,400
You’re just his tennis partner.

521
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:47,560
Do you have to take such good care of him?

522
00:29:47,800 --> 00:29:49,440
I beat him at running this morning.

523
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:52,000
We made a deal that

524
00:29:52,800 --> 00:29:53,880
the loser had to be the other’s servant.

525
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:56,080
Yeah.

526
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:58,080
I shouldn’t have lost.

527
00:29:58,760 --> 00:30:02,600
Now I have to be your servant for five or ten years, or…

528
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:03,480
Bay!

529
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:07,200
Now that Bay is your servant,

530
00:30:07,480 --> 00:30:08,240
what do you call him?

531
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,280
‘Bay-bae’.

532
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:11,480
-Or ‘Baby’.
-Zip it, Zippo.

533
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:33,280
You are…

534
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:34,880
quite a good teacher.

535
00:30:37,760 --> 00:30:38,000
What?

536
00:30:39,680 --> 00:30:40,280
I didn’t do anything.

537
00:30:42,200 --> 00:30:43,800
You make the kids happy.

538
00:30:45,040 --> 00:30:45,880
That’s good enough.

539
00:30:46,920 --> 00:30:48,000
Those teachers at my school

540
00:30:48,400 --> 00:30:49,520
could never be like you.

541
00:30:56,320 --> 00:30:59,280
If studying medicine makes you
suffer and stressed out,

542
00:31:00,120 --> 00:31:01,760
why don’t you try doing something else?

543
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:05,960
My dad wouldn’t allow it.

544
00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:10,240
I got in

545
00:31:10,520 --> 00:31:11,640
but I couldn’t keep going.

546
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:16,840
No wonder he’s ashamed of me.

547
00:31:21,920 --> 00:31:24,520
But your dad wasn’t the one studying.

548
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:26,080
He didn’t know how stressful it was.

549
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:28,840
His opinion can’t be more important than yours, right?

550
00:31:30,120 --> 00:31:33,160
If you kept pushing

551
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:35,960
until you reached your limit,

552
00:31:36,680 --> 00:31:38,360
ultimately, it could be worse.

553
00:31:45,720 --> 00:31:47,920
Then…what do you think I should do?

554
00:31:48,080 --> 00:31:48,480
No idea.

555
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:50,120
What the hell?

556
00:31:59,320 --> 00:32:01,120
Why don’t you open a food stand at my school?

557
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:04,720
So every morning you can give me a ride.

558
00:32:05,320 --> 00:32:07,480
Or you can do it in front of school.

559
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:11,680
So after school, you can give me a ride home

560
00:32:12,200 --> 00:32:13,120
I’m such a genius.

561
00:32:13,120 --> 00:32:14,720
Giving you a ride back and forth?

562
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:18,240
A ride is all you care about?

563
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:23,280
So you will be in my life forever?

564
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:24,200
Why?

565
00:32:24,680 --> 00:32:25,360
Can’t I?

566
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:29,000
Being a teacher is kind of sad, too.

567
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:30,800
The kids come to school,

568
00:32:31,520 --> 00:32:31,880
study,

569
00:32:32,120 --> 00:32:32,560
take exams,

570
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:33,440
and then leave.

571
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:36,320
Only you and I

572
00:32:36,760 --> 00:32:38,000
are still here after decades.

573
